  "notes": "Village of Uehling, modified cash basis, fiscal year ended Sept 30, 2025; basis recorded as cash. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total column of the governmental funds statement (p4: General + Debt Service). Beginning/ending cash = total governmental fund balances (sums of General and Debt Service, computed); the ending balance 435,965 includes due from county treasurer 3,058 (balance sheet cash 392,753 + restricted cash 40,154). Other financing: bond proceeds 300,000 -> debt_proceeds; Other Grants 500 + Sale of Assets 20,000 -> other_financing; transfers (out) 82,171 -> transfers_out. Roll-forward: 400,290 + 312,461 - 515,115 + 300,000 + 20,500 - 82,171 = 435,965. Business-type (Water + Sewer, proprietary statement p11, Total column): operating receipts 125,071 and operating disbursements 160,568 are the printed totals; interest income 8,462, capital outlay 3,350 and debt service 32,962 are printed below the net operating receipts line and recorded with outside_printed_total; transfer from other funds 82,171 -> business_type.transfers_net. Roll-forward: 264,685 + 133,533 - 196,880 + 82,171 = 283,509. Business-type 'Debt service' 32,962 is not split between principal and interest. Balance sheet: Statement of Net Position (p1) Total column (governmental + business-type). Detail: General Fund revenue lines from the p5 budget-and-actual schedule; General Fund disbursements by object from the department schedules pp6-8 (General and Administrative, Street, Parks), which supersede the one-line function disbursements on p5 (not duplicated); Debt Service Fund from p9. Within the G&A schedule all lines carry the department's function (general government) even for Police contract, Garbage and Auditorium expenses, so function totals tie to the statement. Water and Sewer fund columns on p11 not repeated in detail (no separate utility budget schedule). Read pages 1-11 of 11"
